# A repeated component on the LEFT of a swizzle has no meaning: every right side
# is evaluated first, so the two writes to `v.x` have no order to tell them
# apart. Same call simultaneous assignment makes for a repeated plain name, and
# Go and Odin make the other one. A repeat on the RIGHT is plain duplication and
# is fine -- the accepting twin is tests/swizzle.ty, which reads `v.(x, x)`.
# expect: duplicate target 'v.x' in a multi-assign -- every right side is evaluated before any write, so two writes to one place have no order
struct V:
    x: int
    y: int

fn main():
    v := V(1, 2)
    v.(x, x) = v.(y, x)
    println(str(v.x))
